# Normalize text to LF in the index, and check it out as LF everywhere.
#
# LF on checkout is not merely a style preference here. The driver lock file and
# the generated ADBC runtime manifests are compared byte-for-byte against freshly
# serialized content that uses LF: DriverLock.Save and RuntimeManifestGenerator
# both skip writing when the content is unchanged, so that an unchanged resolve
# does not touch a file's timestamp and retrigger downstream incremental builds.
# A CRLF checkout would defeat that comparison and make every resolve report a
# change it did not make.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and archive fixtures must never be translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
